ter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{6}}={x}^{6/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{6}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{6/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6/5+1}}{(\\frac{6}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{11/5}}{\\left(\\frac{11}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{11/5}}{11}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{11/5}}{11}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5{x}^{11/5}}{11}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{11}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{11/5})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{11}\\cdot \\frac{11}{5}{x}^{11/5-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{6/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b264e9f-1b95-5da0-8a5d-53d43f387515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{14/5}}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b264e9f-1b95-5da0-8a5d-53d43f387515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{14/5}}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503898} :answer-field/id #uuid "7639bdc5-e09a-59de-9a6d-7760ce0dd6a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a04ec978-e44a-5fc0-941a-3437fa7bf03c" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}={x}^{9/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{9}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{9/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/5+1}}{(\\frac{9}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{14/5}}{\\left(\\frac{14}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{14/5}}{14}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{14/5}}{14}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5{x}^{14/5}}{14}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{14}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{14/5})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{14}\\cdot \\frac{14}{5}{x}^{14/5-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{9/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a07fc94f-5b6d-5ea9-93c2-7e82f2229b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a07fc94f-5b6d-5ea9-93c2-7e82f2229b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503901} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe4c120-0640-5e64-a81c-759b876005de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a26b65ff-d0b9-55fd-88b5-aeb6bb366617" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}={x}^{8/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{8}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{8/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{8/5+1}}{(\\frac{8}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{13/5}}{\\left(\\frac{13}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5{x}^{13/5}}{13}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{13}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{13/5})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{13}\\cdot \\frac{13}{5}{x}^{13/5-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{8/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9b9a59b-1b30-5f5a-96ca-ff44ec806088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{9/5}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9b9a59b-1b30-5f5a-96ca-ff44ec806088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{9/5}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503915} :answer-field/id #uuid "63f7164e-c9db-55ed-a2c8-afeccd4f032f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a3c79b12-9c14-5549-a389-57292bb076aa" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}={x}^{4/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{4}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{4/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/5+1}}{(\\frac{4}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/5}}{\\left(\\frac{9}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{9/5}}{9}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{9/5}}{9}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5{x}^{9/5}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{9}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{9/5})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{5}{x}^{9/5-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{4/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d457834a-752e-5c58-903b-17caad36936f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d457834a-752e-5c58-903b-17caad36936f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503912} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2aee605-eea6-5ac3-a7aa-7faf947e835f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ab9f77bb-3e23-5176-a3ef-3da256c8008e" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{3}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{3}}={x}^{3/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{3}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[2]{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2+1}}{(\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/2}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{5/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{3/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "181054c9-dbd9-5b5f-a504-255307d12709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{7/3}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "181054c9-dbd9-5b5f-a504-255307d12709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{7/3}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503880} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd4ba04d-d537-57d4-bc2d-b413bfc38584" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e1ab8645-2279-57cf-bef0-772d2fda5a19" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}={x}^{4/3}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{4}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{4/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/3+1}}{(\\frac{4}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/3}}{\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{7/3}}{7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3{x}^{7/3}}{7}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{3{x}^{7/3}}{7}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{7}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7/3})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{7}\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}{x}^{7/3-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{4/3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b19525f-2038-5110-92f7-e19997cc0bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{9/2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b19525f-2038-5110-92f7-e19997cc0bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{9/2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503885} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbecae76-7205-578e-830e-6ad24ef696f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e61be54d-6f89-5777-b645-69438909a48d" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{7}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{7}}={x}^{7/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{7}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[2]{{x}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{7/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/2+1}}{(\\frac{7}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/2}}{\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{9/2}}{9}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{9/2}}{9}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{9/2}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{9}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{9/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}{x}^{9/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{7/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc3fc2e-8291-595d-9efe-37b54c54ec70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507628} {:answer/id #uuid "21b545b6-d2ce-5675-b1f3-a77567c762a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507636} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd6bc83-ee8d-5527-acf0-39f4c02d1429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507789} {:answer/id #uuid "8f99aa38-d301-56e1-857e-d573e65c98ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507801} {:answer/id #uuid "acdc3a68-84af-5610-9099-7c787b10a4a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fd6bc83-ee8d-5527-acf0-39f4c02d1429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507789} :answer-field/id #uuid "44b72334-231e-5d57-bdc0-d2fb9585f9c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "462f5046-e4ee-5f94-8bfd-00082400022c" :question/math-academy-id "q-74956" :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1}=\\frac{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1} & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1)(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1})^{2}-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1) & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}+1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1}+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c9e982-2244-5a23-aac9-ea8f242dfd59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507626} {:answer/id #uuid "2c45373f-5f36-5270-9c27-ce7558fa56c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507653} {:answer/id #uuid "59f30dc1-5f5d-5fdc-a739-06dad6b23c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507728} {:answer/id #uuid "5beae258-194a-5396-abb9-d22777307972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507731} {:answer/id #uuid "824d43de-2c6c-5256-ab7d-e1e81ca546b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5beae258-194a-5396-abb9-d22777307972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186507731} :answer-field/id #uuid "f962e375-138e-5ba3-a11f-61cf507ac9c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6b2bedc8-52f9-5d40-afcd-8617235afd0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129401" :question/problem "Determine $\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nLet's attempt to evaluate the limit approaching $(1,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Taking $x\\to (1,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & =\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 1}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Taking $x\\to (1,0)$ along the path $x=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)\\,\\,\\,x=1}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & =\\lim_{y\\to 0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\lim_{y\\to 0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{y\\to 0}1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510569 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a997286f-4db9-53ee-8849-22966e083d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{113}{280}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a997286f-4db9-53ee-8849-22966e083d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{113}{280}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510578} :answer-field/id #uuid "aac06ef3-2984-5073-a683-edc5d64f81a8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "107b0d08-c0c2-5e3b-a247-c4238dbd6d8f" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{9}{7}\\right)-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{2}{9}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{45}{56}-\\left(-\\frac{2}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{113}{280}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e54747-95d9-5771-963b-49dcf4295948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32e54747-95d9-5771-963b-49dcf4295948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510574} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b44817c-904a-519b-9cfd-76497778888f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "295bc951-4997-5df9-ab67-20bc32e8016a" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{7} & -\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{5}{7} & -\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{4}{5}\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{9}{5}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}-\\left(-\\frac{9}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{55}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "782fb4f6-27a0-5506-9beb-555ca18e4273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1784}{1323}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "782fb4f6-27a0-5506-9beb-555ca18e4273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1784}{1323}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510577} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2dbf444-3856-5b85-8fac-b9843fa4dd21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4f9be678-4285-5f11-ba52-fd42fc00b682" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{9} & -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{4}{9} & -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{8}{3}\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{4}{7}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{2}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{27}-\\left(-\\frac{8}{49}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1784}{1323}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0e44b6c-314a-5501-9b95-06b4d75b5730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{140}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0e44b6c-314a-5501-9b95-06b4d75b5730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{513}{140}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510581} :answer-field/id #uuid "23459979-cbd9-5238-a961-af2acea3f96e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "554f7f1f-b6ff-5426-9de0-5f0d3de16c53" :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{7} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{5} & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{3}{7} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{5} & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{5}{4}\\right)-\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{9}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{28}-\\left(-\\frac{21}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{513}{140}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5c3e732-c3bb-5b5f-b786-d49ab1ea186a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604